  "id": "COMPOUND:30010 - PROTEIN:1959",
  "verbalization": "Michaolide E is implicated in the regulation of Tyrosine--tRNA ligase through a multi-step pathway involving the Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7. This protein is targeted by two distinct compounds: Epifriedelin and 4-Isopropyl-2-cyclohexen-1-one, (R)-(-)-. Both of these molecules are predicted to interact with Tyrosine--tRNA ligase, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Michaolide E influences the activity or function of this enzyme. The evidence indicates that Michaolide E may act as a modulator of the pathway leading to Tyrosine--tRNA ligase, possibly by enhancing or inhibiting the activity of the target proteins. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Michaolide E in the regulation of Tyrosine--tRNA ligase, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
